1266
00:57:37.150 --> 00:57:37.670
Yes.

1267
00:57:38.350 --> 00:57:41.290
Even with breakups and relationships.

1268
00:57:42.530 --> 00:57:44.530
Well, here's the thing about relationships.

1269
00:57:44.810 --> 00:57:49.630
Sometimes, you know, but it takes you a while before you can say it out loud because of the

1270
00:57:49.630 --> 00:57:50.550
ramifications.

1271
00:57:51.170 --> 00:57:51.630
Right.

1272
00:57:51.630 --> 00:57:54.030
But I think you always know.

1273
00:57:54.410 --> 00:58:00.270
Well, I think the women really help Michael know and he is very excited.

1274
00:58:00.710 --> 00:58:07.830
And to thank them for helping him, he's going to buy each one of them an item from Victoria's

1275
00:58:07.830 --> 00:58:08.110
Secret.

1276
00:58:08.350 --> 00:58:09.590
It's what we all wanted.

1277
00:58:10.070 --> 00:58:10.590
Yeah.

1278
00:58:10.850 --> 00:58:16.790
And then there is a talking head that Lee Eisenberg, the writer of this episode, said is one of

1279
00:58:16.790 --> 00:58:22.390
his favorite things he got to write for Steve because Steve's delivery is so great.

1280
00:58:22.770 --> 00:58:31.390
It's the one where he says, most guys want their women and high heels with cleavage and

1281
00:58:31.390 --> 00:58:33.330
wearing skimpy little outfits.

1282
00:58:33.330 --> 00:58:41.290
It's I'm paraphrasing, obviously, but that he thinks a woman looks best absolutely naked.

1283
00:58:41.590 --> 00:58:47.650
He just said when he heard Steve deliver the end of that talking head, he so nailed it.

1284
00:58:47.750 --> 00:58:50.930
It was like it was like a gymnast sticking the landing.

1285
00:58:50.930 --> 00:58:52.530
Yeah, totally.

1286
00:58:53.250 --> 00:58:55.290
Well, Jenna, here's one quick thing.

1287
00:58:55.630 --> 00:59:01.250
There are deleted scenes for this episode and there's some really great ones, but one that

1288
00:59:01.250 --> 00:59:07.390
I found sort of curious and fun is that all the women go into the Victoria's Secrets except

1289
00:59:07.390 --> 00:59:08.770
for Pam and Angela.

1290
00:59:09.130 --> 00:59:14.390
They hang back outside in the mall and there's a beat where you and I look at each other and

1291
00:59:14.390 --> 00:59:17.650
we don't really say anything and we're like, I guess.

1292
00:59:17.650 --> 00:59:19.310
And then we both walk in.

1293
00:59:20.090 --> 00:59:25.450
Well, that's very interesting because we had a fan catch from Sophia Lee.

1294
00:59:26.030 --> 00:59:33.070
And this is one of those moments, Ange, at 20 minutes, 10 seconds, you and I are way back

1295
00:59:33.070 --> 00:59:37.530
in the background of Steve's talking head and we're just walking together through Victoria's

1296
00:59:37.530 --> 00:59:37.810
Secret.

1297
00:59:39.050 --> 00:59:43.790
I feel like we didn't know we were on camera and we're just shopping.

1298
00:59:44.490 --> 00:59:47.330
We were just sort of being chatty in the background.

1299
00:59:47.990 --> 00:59:48.550
Totally.

1300
00:59:48.870 --> 00:59:49.350
That tracks.

1301
00:59:50.050 --> 00:59:53.190
Should we go back to the ladies' lounge at Dunder Mifflin?

1302
00:59:53.330 --> 00:59:53.810
Yes.

1303
00:59:53.950 --> 00:59:59.430
And I have one of my favorite lines from this episode and it's Toby and Paul Lieberstein totally

1304
00:59:59.430 --> 01:00:00.090
crushes it.

1305
01:00:00.430 --> 01:00:00.810
Yes.

1306
01:00:00.990 --> 01:00:03.850
Kevin's like, we should do this more often, guys.

1307
01:00:04.030 --> 01:00:04.970
This is great.

1308
01:00:05.630 --> 01:00:10.070
And Toby goes, I think we hang out an appropriate amount of time.

1309
01:00:10.550 --> 01:00:11.090
Yeah.

1310
01:00:11.530 --> 01:00:12.710
It's so good.

1311
01:00:12.910 --> 01:00:14.050
It's so good.

1312
01:00:14.050 --> 01:00:20.970
And then at 20 minutes, 35 seconds, we have a major old tech alert when Creed enters the

1313
01:00:20.970 --> 01:00:22.650
bathroom with a Walkman.

1314
01:00:22.870 --> 01:00:26.330
With a yellow waterproof Walkman.

1315
01:00:26.330 --> 01:00:27.530
Do you remember those?

1316
01:00:27.830 --> 01:00:28.910
I owned one.

1317
01:00:29.030 --> 01:00:30.090
I owned one.

1318
01:00:30.330 --> 01:00:30.570
I owned one.

1319
01:00:30.570 --> 01:00:31.290
They were the beSt.

1320
01:00:31.570 --> 01:00:34.290
Do you remember the little gray buttons, though, would pop off?

1321
01:00:34.730 --> 01:00:35.150
Yep.

1322
01:00:35.390 --> 01:00:35.630
Yep.

1323
01:00:35.630 --> 01:00:37.450
And you'd have to wedge them back in.

1324
01:00:37.650 --> 01:00:38.730
But it was fun.

1325
01:00:38.910 --> 01:00:41.030
And why did we need a waterproof Walkman?

1326
01:00:41.530 --> 01:00:45.550
Well, the idea was that you were going to get so sweaty while you were working out.

1327
01:00:45.790 --> 01:00:47.350
But I mean, really?

1328
01:00:47.750 --> 01:00:48.070
Okay.

1329
01:00:48.070 --> 01:00:54.650
Well, I guess also Brian Baumgartner told me that when Creed would enter the bathroom with

1330
01:00:54.650 --> 01:00:59.590
that Walkman and be completely stunned and horrified that other people were in there,

1331
01:00:59.730 --> 01:01:00.870
it would make everyone crack up.

1332
01:01:00.930 --> 01:01:05.690
And they had a really, really hard time just getting that, just getting Creed in the room.

1333
01:01:05.730 --> 01:01:07.270
They could not get Creed in.

1334
01:01:07.670 --> 01:01:13.070
I loved Creed's Talking Head, too, because he's listening to music while he's doing the

1335
01:01:13.070 --> 01:01:13.710
Talking Head.

1336
01:01:13.710 --> 01:01:16.470
So he's sort of like yelling over the music he's listening to.

1337
01:01:16.470 --> 01:01:16.910
Yes.

1338
01:01:17.790 --> 01:01:22.950
And I think it's pretty on brand that Creed would go poo in the women's restroom.

1339
01:01:23.210 --> 01:01:24.750
You know those people, Jenna.

1340
01:01:25.230 --> 01:01:26.530
You know those people.

1341
01:01:27.070 --> 01:01:28.570
We've had roommates.

1342
01:01:28.870 --> 01:01:34.810
The roommate that goes and takes a dump in your bathroom instead of theirs, that's Creed.

1343
01:01:35.250 --> 01:01:37.770
Well, now, Ange, we go back to the mall.

1344
01:01:38.870 --> 01:01:42.150
Angela and Michael are sitting.

1345
01:01:42.150 --> 01:01:43.910
And I love the scene so much.

1346
01:01:43.910 --> 01:01:48.470
Michael is dying for Angela to pick something out that he can buy her.

1347
01:01:48.650 --> 01:01:53.970
He has a line where he says, can I please buy you some underwear?

1348
01:01:54.870 --> 01:01:55.410
Yeah.

1349
01:01:55.810 --> 01:02:00.090
So you guys, Steve wanted me to break.

1350
01:02:00.310 --> 01:02:02.750
He was 100% messing with me.

1351
01:02:02.850 --> 01:02:09.170
And I'd been given a very strict note from Tucker Gates and Lee and Gene that they really did not want

1352
01:02:09.170 --> 01:02:11.410
Angela to entertain him at all.

1353
01:02:11.950 --> 01:02:18.310
So I had to sit there very stoic as Steve as Michael just got to throw these lines at me.

1354
01:02:18.430 --> 01:02:22.610
And there's a few in the bloopers because it was really hard to keep it together.

1355
01:02:22.810 --> 01:02:24.510
And Steve was just having a great time.

1356
01:02:24.510 --> 01:02:29.590
I watched the bloopers for this, and there is a great line that didn't make it.

1357
01:02:29.770 --> 01:02:31.070
Is it because I started laughing?

1358
01:02:31.910 --> 01:02:32.190
Yeah.

1359
01:02:32.610 --> 01:02:39.630
But Steve went on to improvise something along the lines of like, pretend it's Christmas and I'm Santa.

1360
01:02:40.090 --> 01:02:42.850
Santa would like to buy you some panties.

1361
01:02:43.270 --> 01:02:43.470
Yes.

1362
01:02:45.250 --> 01:02:47.570
And I started laughing so hard.

1363
01:02:48.270 --> 01:02:50.590
Oh, that was very hard for me to get through.

1364
01:02:50.790 --> 01:02:52.690
And I feel like Steve just started making up things.

1365
01:02:52.770 --> 01:02:53.870
He's like, want a teaback?

1366
01:02:53.970 --> 01:02:55.690
And I was like, I don't even know what that is.

1367
01:02:57.530 --> 01:03:01.690
Well, Pam has a talking head where she explains that she's between boyfriends right now.

1368
01:03:01.870 --> 01:03:03.410
She doesn't need anything sexy.

1369
01:03:03.410 --> 01:03:07.910
So she's going to buy a robe and just turn it into some hand towels.

1370
01:03:08.530 --> 01:03:10.470
I thought that was really industrious of her.

1371
01:03:11.060 --> 01:03:13.030
I thought it was ridiculous.

1372
01:03:13.390 --> 01:03:15.750
I'm like, Pam, just get a pair of comfy sweatpants.

1373
01:03:16.450 --> 01:03:16.990
Right.

1374
01:03:17.150 --> 01:03:17.710
That's true.

1375
01:03:18.010 --> 01:03:18.270
Right.

1376
01:03:18.450 --> 01:03:20.950
And, you know, just go buy some wash rags.

1377
01:03:21.170 --> 01:03:21.630
Wow.

1378
01:03:21.990 --> 01:03:25.550
We have very different responses to this talking head.

1379
01:03:25.570 --> 01:03:27.130
I was offended.

1380
01:03:27.830 --> 01:03:30.050
I love a good bathrobe.

1381
01:03:30.230 --> 01:03:30.990
Come on, Pam.

1382
01:03:31.190 --> 01:03:32.330
Don't cut it up.

1383
01:03:32.750 --> 01:03:33.470
All right.

1384
01:03:33.930 --> 01:03:39.730
Well, now Meredith is driving everyone home from the mall and her tire blows out.

1385
01:03:39.730 --> 01:03:41.970
Oh, probably because she was going too faSt.

1386
01:03:42.450 --> 01:03:47.890
I mean, how many times is my character like, slower, slower, Meredith?

1387
01:03:48.710 --> 01:03:49.150
Yeah.

1388
01:03:49.290 --> 01:03:50.830
Meredith doesn't take care of her car.

1389
01:03:50.990 --> 01:03:52.050
That tire blows out.

1390
01:03:52.330 --> 01:03:54.030
Michael has no idea what to do.

1391
01:03:54.150 --> 01:03:56.270
He's like, Pam, maybe we need a Crescent Allen.

1392
01:03:57.230 --> 01:03:57.670
Yes.

1393
01:03:57.910 --> 01:03:58.450
That's not a thing.

1394
01:03:58.790 --> 01:04:00.770
And Pam is like, I'll do it.

1395
01:04:00.770 --> 01:04:02.570
And she starts to change the tire.

1396
01:04:03.310 --> 01:04:10.310
We had a fan question from Megan Keel, Ciara Begley, Bethany A., Victoria Nash, and Jamie Hahn.

1397
01:04:10.690 --> 01:04:13.050
Does Jenna really know how to change a tire?

1398
01:04:14.750 --> 01:04:15.550
Yes, I do.

1399
01:04:15.890 --> 01:04:16.750
So do I.

1400
01:04:17.010 --> 01:04:19.790
And I've changed one on the side of the road with a friend of mine.

1401
01:04:20.430 --> 01:04:20.850
Same.

1402
01:04:21.110 --> 01:04:21.470
Yes.

1403
01:04:21.590 --> 01:04:23.370
My dad taught me how to change a tire.

1404
01:04:23.570 --> 01:04:24.790
He would make me practice.

1405
01:04:25.410 --> 01:04:32.510
And he would not let me get a car until I knew how to change a tire, check the oil, and replace the fluids.

1406
01:04:32.730 --> 01:04:35.470
I love that our dads taught us how to handle our cars.

1407
01:04:35.470 --> 01:04:37.090
I just think that's so sweet.

1408
01:04:37.870 --> 01:04:47.390
Okay, so now we're back at the office, and you guys, Jim goes to grab a yogurt, and he sees Pam's sketch of Dwight.

1409
01:04:47.750 --> 01:04:49.170
And he knows it's Pam.

1410
01:04:49.530 --> 01:04:55.290
And I just feel like this is just a little moment between the two of them, even though they're not together.

1411
01:04:56.770 --> 01:04:57.250
Yeah.

1412
01:04:57.250 --> 01:04:58.750
I just thought it was really sweet.

1413
01:04:59.630 --> 01:05:11.070
Well, they've purposely not had much Jim-Pam interaction for the last three episodes, because, you know, next week is Beach Games, and we're going to have a big moment.

1414
01:05:11.210 --> 01:05:12.090
Oh, are we?

1415
01:05:12.250 --> 01:05:13.930
And they really wanted that to be a surprise.

1416
01:05:14.870 --> 01:05:16.690
Man, I re-watched Beach Games.

1417
01:05:16.770 --> 01:05:19.910
I know we'll get there, but I was like, whoa, Pam!

1418
01:05:20.570 --> 01:05:28.410
Yeah, but even still, they did want some little moment where you were reminded of the affection of these two characters, and this was it.

1419
01:05:28.530 --> 01:05:29.590
Just him seeing the poster.

1420
01:05:29.730 --> 01:05:31.890
That's all you got in this episode.

1421
01:05:32.130 --> 01:05:35.290
And it inspired him for the tag, and we'll get to that.

1422
01:05:35.530 --> 01:05:36.710
I think so, too.

1423
01:05:36.990 --> 01:05:37.150
Yeah.

1424
01:05:37.270 --> 01:05:44.790
Well, something we haven't talked much about is the Andy Dwight storyline in this episode, where they're going around, and they're hanging up these posters.

1425
01:05:44.790 --> 01:05:54.550
And Dwight is just being so condescending to Andy the whole time, but it's very clear to Andy that this is a drawing of Dwight, so he's going along with it.

1426
01:05:54.730 --> 01:05:54.910
Yeah.

1427
01:05:55.290 --> 01:05:59.110
And he takes extra flyers, says he's going to put them up all over the town.

1428
01:05:59.250 --> 01:06:01.430
And there is a great deleted scene, Jenna.

1429
01:06:01.530 --> 01:06:11.890
It's a quick moment, but as Michael and the ladies are driving back, they come to a red light, and Michael looks out the window and sees one of the flyers on a tree.

1430
01:06:11.890 --> 01:06:16.050
And he looks at it, and then looks to camera and goes, idiot.

1431
01:06:17.790 --> 01:06:18.710
That's brilliant.

1432
01:06:19.130 --> 01:06:23.810
So Andy's having some fun at Dwight's expense, because he's going to just plaster these everywhere.

1433
01:06:24.050 --> 01:06:33.550
And there is a great scene when at 23 minutes, 40 seconds, Andy shows Dwight three musketeers and goes, have these?

1434
01:06:33.730 --> 01:06:35.570
And Dwight's like, no, whole these.

1435
01:06:35.790 --> 01:06:40.730
And he takes the whole thing in true Dwight fashion, just starts chomping down on it.

1436
01:06:40.730 --> 01:06:46.750
Well, in one of the takes, as Rain ate this candy bar this way, he choked and kind of-

1437
01:06:46.750 --> 01:06:47.190
I remember that.

1438
01:06:47.290 --> 01:06:52.690
He choked and coughed, and they loved it so much, they were like, well, you do it in every take.

1439
01:06:53.050 --> 01:06:53.970
That's amazing.

1440
01:06:55.070 --> 01:07:06.590
Well, when Michael and the women get back to the office, Michael asks Phyllis, Karen, and Pam to come into his office while he calls Jan to break up with her.

1441
01:07:07.070 --> 01:07:08.770
Yeah, he's like, I need my girls.

1442
01:07:08.790 --> 01:07:09.770
I love you guys.

1443
01:07:10.790 --> 01:07:15.250
Well, he gets her voicemail, and he leaves a breakup message.

1444
01:07:15.250 --> 01:07:18.410
Oh, and Jenna, your performance as Pam is so great.

1445
01:07:18.650 --> 01:07:19.870
You're like, don't leave a message.

1446
01:07:19.970 --> 01:07:20.450
Oh, God.

1447
01:07:20.630 --> 01:07:25.090
He's like, you don't want him to leave a message, but he does.

1448
01:07:26.070 --> 01:07:30.150
And then before he can finish it, Jan walks in.

1449
01:07:30.670 --> 01:07:32.050
She walks in.

1450
01:07:32.230 --> 01:07:33.390
Can you imagine?

1451
01:07:35.210 --> 01:07:36.750
I can't imagine.

1452
01:07:37.010 --> 01:07:39.950
And then he's just like, all right, buddy, talk to you later.

1453
01:07:40.650 --> 01:07:42.570
Yeah, someone just walked in.

1454
01:07:42.570 --> 01:07:48.030
Oh, and Phyllis and Karen and Pam, they clear the heck out of there.

1455
01:07:48.170 --> 01:07:49.750
They're like, we're getting out of here.

1456
01:07:50.330 --> 01:07:50.650
Yes.

1457
01:07:51.570 --> 01:07:53.690
And Jan then apologizes.

1458
01:07:54.090 --> 01:07:56.170
She says, I don't like how that phone call went earlier.

1459
01:07:56.830 --> 01:07:59.450
So I drove all the way here to say, I'm sorry.

1460
01:07:59.710 --> 01:08:00.930
Can we get some dinner?

1461
01:08:01.690 --> 01:08:03.790
They awkwardly hold hands.

1462
01:08:03.970 --> 01:08:05.150
It's such a weird moment.

1463
01:08:05.490 --> 01:08:05.690
So weird.

1464
01:08:06.590 --> 01:08:09.250
Steve's performance in this scene is so brilliant.

1465
01:08:09.250 --> 01:08:14.910
When she starts listening to the message and he's kind of looking off, he has this expression

1466
01:08:14.910 --> 01:08:16.190
on his face.

1467
01:08:16.570 --> 01:08:17.910
It's just brilliant.

1468
01:08:17.910 --> 01:08:23.250
And he's just saying things like, maybe we could get Italian, Chinese.

1469
01:08:24.730 --> 01:08:30.470
Jan hears the breakup message and she leaves without saying a word.

1470
01:08:30.810 --> 01:08:31.170
Yeah.

1471
01:08:31.170 --> 01:08:36.430
But I went to the blogs of Jenny Tan and Kath.

1472
01:08:36.630 --> 01:08:37.350
What'd they have?

1473
01:08:37.490 --> 01:08:42.290
Well, first of all, Kath said that when they started shooting the scene, Melora had on dark

1474
01:08:42.290 --> 01:08:48.670
colored nail polish and Greg stopped the scene because he didn't think that it fit her character

1475
01:08:48.670 --> 01:08:49.950
and he had them change it.

1476
01:08:50.210 --> 01:08:50.990
Oh, wow.

1477
01:08:50.990 --> 01:08:55.930
And she noted how impressed she was at his attention to detail, that everything mattered.

1478
01:08:56.290 --> 01:08:57.930
The smallest details mattered.

1479
01:08:58.130 --> 01:09:02.990
And I can imagine if that nail polish was distracting to Greg, it might be distracting to an audience

1480
01:09:02.990 --> 01:09:04.930
member and it would take you out of the scene.

1481
01:09:05.090 --> 01:09:08.470
And being in this scene with these two characters was so important.

1482
01:09:09.310 --> 01:09:09.490
Yeah.

1483
01:09:10.250 --> 01:09:13.110
That would have been weird to me to see Jan with dark nail polish.

1484
01:09:13.250 --> 01:09:14.430
I would have been thrown by that.

1485
01:09:14.430 --> 01:09:19.870
Well, Jenny Tan said that while they were shooting this scene, they gave Melora and Steve the

1486
01:09:19.870 --> 01:09:25.970
option of doing alternate endings and that in one, Melora threw something and in another

1487
01:09:25.970 --> 01:09:27.410
one, she growled at him.

1488
01:09:28.070 --> 01:09:29.810
She just growled at the end.

1489
01:09:30.390 --> 01:09:30.890
Growled?

1490
01:09:31.090 --> 01:09:31.590
Growled.

1491
01:09:32.050 --> 01:09:37.390
And then in another one, she broke down crying and they were watching the taping with Jean and

1492
01:09:37.390 --> 01:09:42.790
Lee, the writers, and Jean and Lee asked them their opinion and that she and Kath said that

1493
01:09:42.790 --> 01:09:49.430
they both felt that Jan would be more mad than sad and they were so excited when they saw the final cut

1494
01:09:49.430 --> 01:09:53.770
because they felt like they had a little part in picking the ending of the scene.

1495
01:09:54.290 --> 01:09:55.810
Well, I thought it was the perfect ending.

1496
01:09:56.010 --> 01:10:04.890
I also think that Jan is not going to spiral out in an office where she is everyone superior.

1497
01:10:05.610 --> 01:10:06.050
Yeah.

1498
01:10:06.270 --> 01:10:07.190
And in front of the cameras.

1499
01:10:07.410 --> 01:10:07.870
Oh, yeah.

1500
01:10:07.870 --> 01:10:16.290
I feel like once she got in her car, maybe it was a different story, but she wasn't going to let

1501
01:10:16.290 --> 01:10:18.150
them see too much.

